All right, kids, I gotta get to work.

241
00:15:22,691 --> 00:15:28,198
If I don't input those numbers, it
doesn't make much of a difference.

242
00:15:31,242 --> 00:15:33,370
So, like, you guys all have jobs?

243
00:15:34,162 --> 00:15:35,830
Yeah, we all have jobs.

244
00:15:36,039 --> 00:15:38,666
See, that's how we buy stuff.

245
00:15:40,293 --> 00:15:41,586
Yeah, I'm an actor.

246
00:15:41,795 --> 00:15:44,005
Wow. Would I have seen you in anything?

247
00:15:44,214 --> 00:15:46,549
Oh, I doubt it. Mostly regional work.

248
00:15:46,758 --> 00:15:50,345
Unless you happened to catch the
Wee One's production of <i>Pinocchio.</i>

249
00:15:50,595 --> 00:15:53,139
"Look, Geppeto. I'm a real live boy."

250
00:15:55,975 --> 00:15:57,685
I will not take this abuse.

251
00:15:57,936 --> 00:15:59,854
You're right. I'm sorry.

252
00:16:00,271 --> 00:16:02,982
<i>♪ Once I was a wooden
boy, a little wooden boy ♪</i>

253
00:16:07,070 --> 00:16:09,530
MONICA: So how are you doing today?
Did you sleep okay?

254
00:16:09,614 --> 00:16:12,951
Did you talk to Barry?
I can't stop smiling.

255
00:16:13,743 --> 00:16:17,622
I can see that. You look like you
slept with a hanger in your mouth.

256
00:16:22,877 --> 00:16:26,339
I know. He's just so…

257
00:16:26,506 --> 00:16:28,056
Remember you and Tony De Marco?

258
00:16:28,258 --> 00:16:32,262
-Oh, yeah.
-Well, it's like that. With feelings.

259
00:16:33,138 --> 00:16:34,806
Oh, wow, are you in trouble!

260
00:16:35,473 --> 00:16:39,269
Okay, okay.
I am just going to get up, go to work,

261
00:16:39,436 --> 00:16:42,148
and not think about him all day.

262
00:16:42,314 --> 00:16:45,276
Or else I'm just gonna
get up and go to work.

263
00:16:45,443 --> 00:16:47,069
-Oh, wish me luck!
-What for?

264
00:16:47,278 --> 00:16:50,573
I'm gonna go get one of those job things.

265
00:16:58,539 --> 00:17:01,167
-Hey, Monica.
-Hey, Franny. Welcome back.

266
00:17:01,333 --> 00:17:02,835
How was Florida?

267
00:17:03,002 --> 00:17:04,336
You had sex, didn't you?

268
00:17:06,213 --> 00:17:07,256
How do you do that?

269
00:17:08,382 --> 00:17:12,178
-So, who?
-You know Paul?

270
00:17:12,720 --> 00:17:14,305
Paul, the wine guy?

271
00:17:14,472 --> 00:17:16,056
Oh, yeah, I know Paul.

272
00:17:18,601 --> 00:17:21,103
You mean, you know Paul like I know Paul?

273
00:17:21,312 --> 00:17:23,606
Are you kidding? I take credit for Paul.

274
00:17:23,772 --> 00:17:27,902
Before me, there was no
snap in his turtle for two years.

275
00:17:31,155 --> 00:17:33,699
Of course it was a line.

276
00:17:34,116 --> 00:17:36,785
Why?
Why would anybody do something like that?

277
00:17:36,994 --> 00:17:40,247
We're looking for an answer
more sophisticated than:

278
00:17:40,414 --> 00:17:42,333
"To get you into bed."

279
00:17:43,292 --> 00:17:44,960
Is it me?

280
00:17:45,127 --> 00:17:48,672
Is it like I have some sort
of beacon that only dogs,

281
00:17:48,839 --> 00:17:51,467
and men with severe
emotional problems can hear?

282
00:17:51,675 --> 00:17:53,675
All right, come here. Give me your feet.

283
00:18:01,102 --> 00:18:02,952
I just thought he was nice, you know?

284
00:18:05,815 --> 00:18:08,276
I can't believe you
didn't know it was a line.

285
00:18:13,156 --> 00:18:14,199
Guess what.

286
00:18:14,366 --> 00:18:16,159
-You got a job?
-Are you kidding?

287
00:18:16,326 --> 00:18:17,994
I'm trained for nothing.

288
00:18:19,829 --> 00:18:21,879
I was laughed out of 12 interviews today.

289
00:18:22,040 --> 00:18:23,590
Yet you're surprisingly upbeat.

290
00:18:23,792 --> 00:18:27,295
Well, you would be too if you
found Joan and David boots on sale

291
00:18:27,462 --> 00:18:29,214
50 percent off.

292
00:18:29,422 --> 00:18:31,216
Oh, how well you know me.

293
00:18:32,884 --> 00:18:35,303
They're my new "I don't
need a job or my parents.

294
00:18:35,554 --> 00:18:37,722
I've got great boots" boots.

295
00:18:39,099 --> 00:18:41,309
-How'd you pay for them?
-Uh, credit card.

296
00:18:41,851 --> 00:18:43,520
And who pays for that?

297
00:18:44,187 --> 00:18:46,273
Um, my father.

298
00:18:48,858 --> 00:18:51,152
You can't live off your
parents your whole life.

299
00:18:51,236 --> 00:18:54,906
I know that.
That's why I was getting married.

300
00:18:55,282 --> 00:18:58,367
Give her a break. It's hard being
on your own for the first time.

301
00:18:58,451 --> 00:18:59,953
-Thank you.
-You're welcome.

302
00:19:00,120 --> 00:19:02,831
I remember when I first
came to this city, I was 14.

303
00:19:02,998 --> 00:19:05,948
My mom had killed herself and
my stepdad was back in prison.

304
00:19:06,042 --> 00:19:08,092
And I got here, and I
didn't know anybody.

305
00:19:08,253 --> 00:19:11,703
I ended up living with this albino
guy who was cleaning windshields

306
00:19:11,799 --> 00:19:15,595
outside Port Authority.
And then he killed himself.

307
00:19:16,345 --> 00:19:17,838
And then I found aromatherapy.

308
00:19:17,922 --> 00:19:20,182
So believe me, I know
exactly how you feel.

309
00:19:24,312 --> 00:19:27,064
The word you're looking for is:

310
00:19:27,648 --> 00:19:28,899
"Anyway…"

311
00:19:33,070 --> 00:19:34,196
All right. You ready?

312
00:19:34,363 --> 00:19:36,213
-I don't think so.
-ROSS: Oh, come on.

313
00:19:36,407 --> 00:19:37,825
Cut. Cut.

314
00:19:38,034 --> 00:19:40,995
ALL: Cut, cut, cut.

315
00:19:42,622 --> 00:19:45,541
-ROSS: Hey.
-MONICA: All right.

316
00:19:45,791 --> 00:19:47,501
Welcome to the real world.

317
00:19:47,710 --> 00:19:50,463
It sucks. You're gonna love it.

318
00:19:51,339 --> 00:19:54,089
[FRANCIS SCOTT KEY'S
"STAR-SPANGLED BANNER" PLAYS ON TV]

319
00:19:57,386 --> 00:20:00,723
Well, that's it.
You gonna crash on the couch?

320
00:20:00,931 --> 00:20:04,268
-No. No, I gotta go home sometime.
-Are you gonna be okay?

321
00:20:04,435 --> 00:20:05,936
Yeah.

322
00:20:06,979 --> 00:20:08,856
Look what I just found on the floor.

323
00:20:11,150 --> 00:20:12,401
What?

324
00:20:12,860 --> 00:20:14,362
That's Paul's watch.

325
00:20:14,528 --> 00:20:16,678
You can just put it
back where you found it.

326
00:20:18,240 --> 00:20:21,702
Oh, boy. All right.
Good night, everybody.

327
00:20:21,869 --> 00:20:22,995
ROSS, RACHEL: Good night.

328
00:20:23,079 --> 00:20:24,998
[WATCH CRACKS]

329
00:20:28,877 --> 00:20:30,295
[DOOR CLOSES]

330
00:20:31,421 --> 00:20:33,090
-Hmm.
-Hmm.

331
00:20:34,216 --> 00:20:35,550
-Oh, sorry.
-No. Oh, no. Go.

332
00:20:35,634 --> 00:20:37,594
-No, have it, really.
-Split it?

333
00:20:37,761 --> 00:20:39,763
-Okay.
-Okay.

334
00:20:41,682 --> 00:20:42,724
Thanks.

335
00:20:43,433 --> 00:20:47,020
You probably didn't know this,
but back in high school I had

336
00:20:47,187 --> 00:20:49,022
a major crush on you.

337
00:20:50,482 --> 00:20:51,650
I knew.

338
00:20:52,025 --> 00:20:54,277
You did? Oh.

339
00:20:55,070 --> 00:20:58,073
I figured you thought I was
Monica's geeky older brother.

340
00:20:58,824 --> 00:21:00,826
-I did.
-Oh.

341
00:21:05,455 --> 00:21:07,290
Listen, do you think…

342
00:21:07,457 --> 00:21:10,961
And try not to let my vulnerability
become any kind of a factor here.

343
00:21:13,046 --> 00:21:16,925
Do you think it would be okay
if I ask you out sometime, maybe?

344
00:21:18,176 --> 00:21:20,011
Yeah.

345
00:21:20,470 --> 00:21:21,763
Maybe.

346
00:21:22,764 --> 00:21:24,599
Okay.

347
00:21:29,354 --> 00:21:31,815
Okay, maybe I will.

348
00:21:34,151 --> 00:21:35,610
[RACHEL CHUCKLES]

349
00:21:35,777 --> 00:21:37,904
-Good night.
-Good night.

350
00:21:40,908 --> 00:21:42,910
[DOOR OPENS, CLOSES]

351
00:21:48,374 --> 00:21:50,376
[DOOR OPENS]

352
00:21:51,461 --> 00:21:53,171
See you.

353
00:21:53,671 --> 00:21:54,714
ROSS: Mm-hm.

354
00:21:54,881 --> 00:21:57,300
Wait, wait. Hey, what's with you?

355
00:21:59,594 --> 00:22:02,263
I just grabbed a spoon.

356
00:22:10,438 --> 00:22:11,988
Can't believe what I'm hearing.

357
00:22:12,148 --> 00:22:13,899
<i>♪ I can't believe, what I'm hearing here ♪</i>

358
00:22:13,983 --> 00:22:16,383
-What? I said you had…
<i>-♪ What? I said you had… ♪</i>

359
00:22:17,236 --> 00:22:19,697
-Would you stop?
-Oh, was I doing it again?

360
00:22:19,906 --> 00:22:21,741
ALL: Yes.

361
00:22:22,784 --> 00:22:24,786
WOMAN: Would anybody like more coffee?

362
00:22:26,662 --> 00:22:29,123
Did you make it or
are you just serving it?

363
00:22:29,290 --> 00:22:32,585
-I'm just serving it.
-CHANDLER: I'll have a cup of coffee.

364
00:22:33,044 --> 00:22:34,295
Kids, new dream.

365
00:22:35,046 --> 00:22:38,382
I'm in Las Vegas. I'm Liza Minnelli.

